# heartwall (Rodinia)

Tracks the inner and outer walls of a mouse heart in an ultrasound video.

## Benchmark source

Rodinia Benchmark Suite 3.1 (http://lava.cs.virginia.edu/wiki/rodinia).

Contact (for the original code):

- Ke Wang: kw5na@virginia.edu
- Shuai Che: sc5nf@cs.virginia.edu
- Kevin Skadron: skadron@cs.virginia.edu

## Build

```bash
make
```

`make` builds `heartwall_baseline.exe`, `heartwall_pim.exe`, `heartwall_pim_fast.exe`.

| Executable | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `heartwall_baseline.exe` | CPU baseline |
| `heartwall_pim.exe` | PUD-instrumented version; also executes every bbop on the CPU |
| `heartwall_pim_fast.exe` | PUD-instrumented version without CPU execution of bbops (used by `scripts/run_workloads.sh`) |

`make` also builds the AVI helper library in `AVI/`.

## Run

```
./heartwall_<version>.exe <input.avi> <num_frames> <num_threads>
```

The paper processes 20 frames of the 3840x2160 video `test_4k.avi` with
eight threads:

```bash
./heartwall_pim_fast.exe /path/to/test_4k.avi 20 8
```

The video is not redistributed. `docs/DATASETS.md` lists its SHA-256
checksum; without it, the frozen heartwall results in `reference/results/`
are used.

## Output

The PUD versions write `bbop_statistics.csv`, `transposition.csv`, and
`bbop_resolution.csv` to the working directory. See `../README.md` for their
format.
